  nodeName: GLP-1 Binds to GLP-1R
  nodePreview: {fileID: 0}
  nodeNumber: 0
  nodeNexus: 1
  nodeType: 0
  nodeConstituents: 0500000006000000
  nodePositions: []
  nodeAbstract: 
  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: What happens between GLP-1 and GLP-1R? Why is this interaction important?
    basic: "GLP-1R and GLP-1 bind together, causing GLP-1R to change to and stay
      in its active form. \nDrugs designed to treat diabetes mimic the interaction
      between GLP-1 and GLP-1R."
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "5 amino acid residues on the extracellular domain and 11 on the transmembrane
      domain form the binding pocket for GLP-1. GLP-1 is anchored in its place through
      hydrophobic and hydrophilic interactions between its residues and GLP-1R. \nThese
      interactions stabilize the active conformation of GLP-1R and allow multiple
      activations of G protein complexes. "
  nodeSpriteLayer: []
